<unit id="028a88ba-62a9-4fa4-99c1-53e71276c877">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 2</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: # </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Character information</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="584b9c43-d7c7-457f-b7f6-e071dc1372c3">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 4</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Author: Cyrille Bougot</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="6ecb5440-2284-471a-a0fd-5d62a9fe9eb0">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 5</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA compatibility: 2024.1 and beyond</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="0d74c49a-6cb2-4a4b-9b57-30c0c3b08275">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 7</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>This add-on allows to present in a message various information about a character.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="bf6ae32a-16ff-4bb3-a0fa-53c91ba8af69">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 8</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>It also allows to customize the information reported on a character when using review cursor character navigation commands or multiple presses of the review character command.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="957ed949-a96c-44c3-8b50-9acaf9895fd2">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 10</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ### </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Features</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="0a6f0bd0-b677-404c-a20b-cb1921e779d4">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 12</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Display detailed information on a character, e.g. Unicode name, number, CLDR, symbol name, etc.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="796403da-d657-4fee-9cdb-51e860822978">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 13</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>This information can be displayed either at the location of the review cursor or at the location of the system cursor.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="b90614cf-6024-402a-8cc2-101bcbdc250f">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 14</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Customize the reported information when pressing `numpad2`.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="c75b6643-e5ad-402f-a086-92151c1412d5">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 15</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Use the same custom information when moving the review cursor by character.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="614f7ad6-5787-4427-a172-742d34684629">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 17</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Commands</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="f02da979-a3cb-4433-8747-02013f0abc96">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 19</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>`Numpad2` (all keyboard layouts) or `NVDA+.` (laptop layout): when pressed 4 times, displays information about the character of the current navigator object where the review cursor is situated. This command can also be customized in the settings of the add-on.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="c330dcee-bb34-4ffe-97c9-1993b6f0b64e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 20</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Unassigned: Presents a message with detailed information on the character where the review cursor is situated. If you feel uncomfortable with the four press gesture, you may use this command instead.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="35d2eaf2-8fd0-4abc-9ef0-7a705af40fbd">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 21</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Unassigned: Presents a message with detailed information on the character at the position of the caret (works only in places where there is a caret).</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="05d964b3-13bc-455a-8862-8c4cc9f7626a">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 22</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Unassigned: Opens Character Information add-on settings.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="483c9390-3a7c-4f94-9b47-a00677f64dac">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 24</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>The unassigned commands need first to be assigned in the Input gestures dialog to be used.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="4dede572-2e5b-44f1-8220-6d729c184e7f">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 26</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Detailed information on a character</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="765210f1-963f-4a54-bdff-8d38742d20a1">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 28</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>The presented information include the following sections:</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="a34ca4cb-4077-45df-874f-f90d95d33f04">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 30</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Unicode: information from Unicode norm, i.e. name, CLDR name, value, block, etc.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="b5ecc7cf-f219-4286-9b98-8b7257eff315">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 31</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>MS font, only for characters written with proprietary Microsoft fonts (Symbol, Wingding 1, 2, 3 and Webding): name and information about the equivalent Unicode character.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="590ddc56-6b78-41ad-8fa2-75bc8614706b">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 32</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA symbol description: information allowing to understand how NVDA reports the symbol description. NVDA uses the information in the top most rows containing available information to provide the description of a symbol.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="faef0e73-4ad5-489d-9400-18f874fff61c">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 33</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA character description: information allowing to understand how NVDA reports the character description (e.g. "alpha" for "A"). NVDA uses the information in the top most rows containing available information to provide the description of a character.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="afdd73f9-fa3a-45bb-9eb6-f0405ad2f284">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 35</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>The provided information in the Unicode section is in English since it is part of Unicode norm. If a local translation exists for this add-on, the information is also provided alongside with English.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="1a0934aa-722b-451e-9b46-c2f265a2c6c7">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 37</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Regarding NVDA symbol description section: This add-on does not yet support custom symbol dictionaries (introduced in NVDA 2024.4).</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="93febc3e-f712-4132-84f2-d7eabc62f6a9">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 38</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>They already appear in the list "Options used to compute the symbol" but not in the table itself.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="bbd788b3-c7b5-4a8d-92a8-b4cd2dbde66c">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 40</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Settings</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="38d6456a-780e-4046-a32a-c3b82a33b3f8">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 42</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>This add-on has its own category in NVDA's settings dialog where you can configure the following options.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="76f01b23-b811-417e-a20d-3e06b03ae749">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 44</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ### </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Action for multiple presses of the report review character command</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="c3548594-6ceb-476c-91dc-da1c5cc1d70d">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 46</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>The three combo boxes of this group allow to customize what is reported by the report review character command (`numpad2`) when using two, three or four presses.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="febb863e-733c-479a-992e-fad073e9d139">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 47</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>By default, NVDA reports the character description on second press and its numeric value, decimal and hexadecimal, on third press.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="28459784-e384-4357-942d-fd77d532810c">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 48</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>You can change what is reported on the character at the position of the review cursor upon multiple presses.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="097c8d86-3557-4f27-af46-8612950b96ac">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 49</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>For example, you can report its CLDR English name on second press, its Unicode name on third press and display detailed information on it on fourth press.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="72c9623d-1310-4c1a-b7e2-7c87c4377eea">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 51</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ### </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Remember these action during character navigation</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="6bb7d276-dade-4eed-a7b8-d3a84801534e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 53</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>When you have reported specific information with the report review character command (`numpad2`) called multiple times, you may want to continue reporting the same information while navigating with the review cursor (`numpad1` and `numpad3`).</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="69abc2f1-985d-4ae0-a7c8-9136da7c4a7d">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 54</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Checking this option will allow you to do it, as long as you navigate with the review cursor by character just after a multiple press of `numpad2`.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="0d44ebc6-b130-4e1f-86aa-9645092668ce">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 56</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Change log</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="86e4a6dc-5555-4778-b1ec-aca90493d6d9">
